{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/performance"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"title":"Performance"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Guides","anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking"]}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record is data the linker places in a section, so nothing runs for it at launch. Reading a set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"walks every loaded image’s section once and calls the accessor of each record of the set’s kind."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"That’s linear in the records the program holds, and the reads aren’t cached, so read a set once"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where the program starts and keep the array. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetsPerformanceTests"},{"type":"text","text":" checks the scaling in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"release builds: reading 3,000 records costs no more than about 10 times reading 300."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The build pays for each marked declaration: the macro’s expansion and the record it compiles to.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"That cost is also linear while the records are spread across files, as they are in an app.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Thousands of records in one file take the compiler much longer, so generated registries are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"better split.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Measured","type":"heading","anchor":"Measured","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"just benchmark"},{"text":" measures both in a SwiftPM package of generated records, against the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declarations without the macro. These figures are from an M1 Ultra with Swift 6.4.2, in a debug","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"build, with each size’s records split across 10 files:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Records"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Build time the records add","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Per record"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading every record (release)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"100"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2.6 s","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"26 ms"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"77 µs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1,000"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"4.2 s","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.3 ms"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"242 µs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"10,000"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"50 s"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"5.0 ms","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2.0 ms"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row","type":"table","alignments":["right","right","right","right"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The 100-record row is mostly the macro plugin’s start-up, paid once per module that uses it. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read also has a fixed part, the walk over every image the process has loaded, which is about"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"70 µs on macOS. In a single file, 10,000 records added 111 s to the build instead of 50 s."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"What records cost as an app grows: nothing at launch, a walk of the records when a set is read,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a few milliseconds of build time per marked declaration.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/UniqueKeys":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Make two records of one kind with the same key fail to build, within one executable or library.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Unique keys","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/uniquekeys","kind":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","type":"topic","title":"Platforms and linking","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/DeclaringAKind":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it."}],"title":"Declaring a kind","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","kind":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/ReplacingARegistry":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","type":"topic","title":"Replacing a hand-written registry","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"themselves.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect."}],"type":"topic","title":"Finding records","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","type":"topic","title":"LinkerSets","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why."}],"title":"What the macros refuse","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","kind":"article"}}}